<title>UK: Main Novorossiisk crude line reopens on schedule.</title>
<headline>Main Novorossiisk crude line reopens on schedule.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-08-04</dateline>
<text>
<p>The main crude pipeline to Russian Black Sea terminal Novorossiisk reopened following repairs as expected late on Friday, a reliable shipping source said.</p>
<p>The 90,000 tonne per day line had been closed since last Tuesday.</p>
<p>A smaller pipeline to the port had reopened on Thursday.</p>
<p>Operations at other Black Sea and Baltic ports -- Batumi, Odessa, Tuapse and Ventspils -- which handle Russian crude were all running as normal on Monday, the shipping source said.</p>
<p>--London newsroom +44 171 542 6280</p>
</text>
